      "text": "\n\n# Release Plan: New Authentication Flow (v2)\n\n**Owner:** Platform/Auth Team  \n**Status:** Draft \u2014 pending security review sign-off  \n**Target date:** T+14 days from security review completion  \n**Affected services:** `auth-service`, `api-gateway`, `session-store`, `web-client`, `mobile-sdk`\n\n---\n\n## 1. Scope\n\nReplace the legacy session-cookie auth flow with the new token-based flow (short-lived access tokens + rotating refresh tokens, PKCE for OAuth2 leg, device-bound refresh tokens). The old flow remains available behind a flag during the migration window.\n\n**Out of scope:** SSO/IdP integration changes, MFA policy changes, billing/entitlement logic.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Feature Flags\n\n| Flag | Scope | Default | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `auth.v2.enabled` | Per-tenant (config DB) | `false` | Master switch for new flow |\n| `auth.v2.legacy_fallback` | Per-tenant | `true` | Allow old flow if v2 token issuance fails |\n| `auth.v2.mobile_only` | Per-tenant | `false` | Restrict v2 to mobile SDK only (staging) |\n| `auth.v2.force_logout_on_switch` | Per-tenant | `false` | Force re-auth when tenant flips flag |\n| `auth.v2.telemetry.verbose` | Global | `false` | Emit detailed auth telemetry (rate-limited) |\n\n**Flag management:** Flags live in the tenant config table, not in code. Changes propagate via the existing config-push channel (\u2264 30 s latency). No redeploy required to toggle.\n\n**Constraint:** `auth.v2.enabled` and `auth.v2.legacy_fallback` must never both be `false` for a tenant. The config service enforces this invariant; the API gateway rejects a config push that violates it.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Security Review\n\n**Must complete before any traffic is routed to v2.**\n\n- [ ] **Threat model review** \u2014 Auth team + Security team walk through the new token lifecycle, refresh-token rotation, and device-binding logic. Documented in `docs/security/auth-v2-threat-model.md`.\n- [ ] **Token format & entropy audit** \u2014 Confirm access tokens are \u2265 256-bit random, refresh tokens are opaque (not JWT",
      "text_preview": "\n\n# Release Plan: New Authentication Flow (v2)\n\n**Owner:** Platform/Auth Team  \n**Status:** Draft \u2014 pending security review sign-off  \n**Target date:** T+14 days from security review completion  \n**Affected services:** `auth-service`, `api-gateway`, `session-store`, `web-client`, `mobile-sdk`\n\n---\n\n## 1. Scope\n\nReplace",
